Key to families of the Aphyllophorales (literally “not bearing gills”)
The key uses macroscopic characteristics to key out to Friesian family

titre$families of the Aphyllophorales
com$Adapt GF nov 2015
rem$LANGUE$Anglais
1,0$ Source : Key to families of the Aphyllophorales (literally “not bearing gills”)  http://www.utm.utoronto.ca/
1,0$


1,0 $Fruiting body red-brown or yellow, at least when young. Turns black with a drop of 2-3% KOH, pore  surface not white or tan (micr. Usually with setae, no clamps ) $Hymenochaetaceae
1,2 $Fruiting body does not turn black in KOH (micr. characteristics otherwise).
2,0 $Hymenophore with pores $Polyporaceae s.l.
2,3 $Hymenophore smooth or with teeth or upright branches
3,0 $Hymenophore smooth $Corticiaceae and Thelephoraceae
3,4 $Hymenophore with teeth or upright branches
4,0 $Hymenophore with downward pointing teeth $Hydnaceae
4,0 $Hymenophore with upright branches $Clavariaceae
